00:10:02,980 --> 00:10:12,779
The FLSA, the Fair Labor Standards Act, requires that employers pay any hours, actual hours worked over 40 at time and a half.

196
00:10:12,779 --> 00:10:19,779
For years, the city has considered vacation, six time, and comp time as actual hours worked.

197
00:10:19,779 --> 00:10:22,779
We're not required to do that per the FLSA.

198
00:10:22,779 --> 00:10:30,180
So we didn't turn a lot at thinking that we've implemented in the last year and a half, very competitive market salaries.

199
00:10:30,180 --> 00:10:34,180
And that this is something we weren't required to do.

200
00:10:34,180 --> 00:10:40,180
When we thought about how to communicate it to employees, I thought Cindy Banner worked him up with the best explanation.

201
00:10:40,180 --> 00:10:45,580
We're just no longer going to pay half time if you take vacations sick and comp time.

202
00:10:45,580 --> 00:10:50,779
So employees are still going to be paid for everything they actually work over 40.

203
00:10:50,779 --> 00:10:58,180
But if you take, for example, made out vacation day and you work a couple of extra hours, those two extra hours will not be time and a half.

204
00:10:58,180 --> 00:10:59,980
They will be straight pay.

205
00:10:59,980 --> 00:11:04,779
And how does this deal with holidays relative to overtime?

206
00:11:04,779 --> 00:11:08,580
We've got a lot of discussion about that and we're leaving that where it is.

207
00:11:08,580 --> 00:11:17,580
So we're still going to consider that when we consider overtime pay, this is only going to involve vacation sick and comp.

208
00:11:17,580 --> 00:11:22,340
It's going to save the city about $25,000 a year.

209
00:11:22,340 --> 00:11:26,940
We're not required to pay overtime pay when there's a holiday in the week, but we choose to.

210
00:11:26,940 --> 00:11:36,539
We chose to, because we felt like it has an additional incentive for employees to work on that holiday.

211
00:11:36,539 --> 00:11:45,940
